SPARTA (24 Sep 2025)
Running on 1 MPI task(s)
################################################################################
# thermal gas in a 3d box with a moving piston wall
#
# Regression coverage for the surf_collide piston model, which is not used by
# any other example.  The xlo box boundary is treated as a surface and assigned
# a piston collision model (a subsonic pressure boundary condition); incident
# particles collide as if the wall moves with velocity Vwall, so the gas
# expands through the xlo boundary and cools.
#
# Note:
#  - The "comm/sort" option to the "global" command is used to match MPI runs.
#  - The "twopass" option is used to match Kokkos runs.
# The "comm/sort" and "twopass" options should not be used for production runs.
################################################################################

seed	    	    12345
dimension   	    3
global              gridcut 1.0e-5 comm/sort yes

boundary	    sr r r

create_box  	    0 0.0001 0 0.0001 0 0.0001
Created orthogonal box = (0 0 0) to (0.0001 0.0001 0.0001)
create_grid 	    10 10 10
Created 1000 child grid cells
  CPU time = 0.00100475 secs
  create/ghost percent = 84.8601 15.1399
balance_grid        rcb part
Balance grid migrated 0 cells
  CPU time = 0.000203211 secs
  reassign/sort/migrate/ghost percent = 56.0103 0.474876 10.9891 32.5258

species		    ar.species Ar
mixture		    air Ar vstream 0.0 0.0 0.0 temp 273.15

global              nrho 7.07043E22
global              fnum 7.07043E6

create_particles    air n 10000 twopass
Created 10000 particles
  CPU time = 0.0019818 secs

# xlo boundary acts as a piston moving inward at 100 m/s
surf_collide        pist piston 100.0
bound_modify        xlo collide pist

compute             temp temp
stats		    100
stats_style	    step cpu np c_temp
timestep 	    7.00E-9
run 		    1000
